{
  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts opened the oral argument for case\u202f06\u2011134, The Permanent Mission of India to the United Nations et\u202fal. v. City of New\u202fYork."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "John J.P. Howley",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to John J.P. Howley, the case involves tax\u2011enforcement lawsuits; if jurisdiction exists, the court would decide only whether a tax is owed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justices asked whether the issue falls within the property\u2011right exception."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justices asked whether the lien is an interest in land that runs with the land."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether the dispute is a question of state law or federal law."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justices questioned the distinction between a mortgage and a tax lien."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether, under the respondent\u2019s theory, the lien would be unenforceable."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The respondent argued that a lien is a form of intangible personal property\u2014a claim against the property."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondent, the respondent noted that the inability to foreclose does not eliminate a property right in the lien."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy raised the issue of easements and asked how they relate to property rights."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked whether a claim in immovable property is required for a property\u2011right dispute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Cardozo",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dab354da5bab5bf176bb9a36622a4a1a803fd15d9cf8ee3e8f9f5bd9c328e2b7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dab354da5bab-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Cardozo, mr.\u202fCardozo, speaking for the petitioner, said the lien could wipe out the value of the property, making the property\u2011right claim critical."
      }
    ],
